2. Use parameterized queries or safer string formatting methods to construct URLs for API requests.
3. Avoid using `os.system()` with user-controlled input; consider using more secure alternatives like `subprocess.run()`.
4. Implement proper exception handling to avoid unhandled exceptions.
5. Ensure all dependencies are up-to-date and free from known vulnerabilities.
6. Consider refactoring the code to use local variables instead of global ones to reduce state-related issues.
