**Recommendations:**
1. Use parameterized queries or an ORM to construct SQL statements safely.
2. Validate and sanitize all user inputs before using them in any database operations.
3. Implement proper authorization checks to ensure users can only access data they are authorized to see.
4. Add robust error handling to prevent the exposure of sensitive information.
5. Consider hashing or encrypting sensitive data stored in the database.
</analysis>

