CWEs: CWE-89 (SQL Injection) - High Confidence, CWE-209 (Information Disclosure Through Error Message) - Medium Confidence, CWE-754 (Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions) - Medium Confidence

**Recommendations:**
1. Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection.
2. Implement proper error handling by catching specific exceptions and logging errors appropriately.
3. Ensure all database connections are closed after use to free up resources.
</analysis>

