```
- The code skips the initial "ng " prefix and finds the first space. It calculates the length up to this space.
- Memory is allocated for `pkt->ref` with the calculated length plus one (for the null terminator) and checked.
- The `memcpy` copies the substring into `pkt->ref`, and a null terminator is added.

```c
	line = ptr + 1;
	if (!(ptr = strchr(line, '\n')))
