   - The code connects to the GPSD service on localhost without any form of encryption or authentication.
   - An attacker with access to the local network can potentially intercept or manipulate the communication.
   - Confidence Level: Medium

2. **Command Injection Risk in Protocol Handling (CWE-78)**
   - Although the function sends specific commands to the GPSD service, there is no validation or sanitization of these commands.
