### Notes

- **Hash Function:** The effectiveness of this lookup mechanism heavily depends on the quality of the `hash()` function. Ideally, it should distribute hash values uniformly across the range `[0, MAX_HASH_VALUE]` to minimize collisions and ensure efficient lookups.
  
- **Collision Handling:** This implementation does not handle hash collisions (i.e., different codes producing the same hash value). It only checks if the code at the calculated index matches the input. If a collision occurs, the function will incorrectly return `0`.

- **Performance Consideration:** The use of a direct array lookup based on a hash can be very fast compared to linear search methods, especially when the hash distribution is good and collisions are rare.

