The provided code appears to be vulnerable to Command Injection (CWE-78). This vulnerability arises due to the lack of proper sanitization or escaping of user input (vdisk_name) in the construction of the ssh_cmd variable. An attacker could potentially manipulate the vdisk_name parameter to execute arbitrary commands on the system by injecting shell metacharacters within the parameter.

Here's an example of a command injection attempt:
```bash
vdisk_name = "some_vdisk'; rm -rf /; ls"
```
In this instance, the attacker can execute the 'rm -rf /' command which would delete all files in the root directory, followed by an 'ls' command to verify if the attack was successful. To mitigate this risk, it is recommended to use parameterized queries or escape special characters in user input before using them in shell commands.

