By specifying relative paths in the command, there is a possibility that an attacker could traverse the file system by using path traversal techniques (such as "../") to access or manipulate sensitive files within the host system.

This vulnerability may not be critical, but it can still lead to unintended data exposure or modification if proper input validation and sanitization are not implemented.

