The _delete_host function constructs an ssh_cmd string by concatenating the 'svctask rmhost' command with the user-provided host_name variable without any input validation or sanitization. This could potentially allow attackers to inject additional commands into the ssh_cmd string, altering the intended behavior of the function. For example, an attacker might attempt to execute arbitrary system commands by manipulating the host_name parameter.

While the risk is reduced in this case due to the function's _run_ssh method handling the command execution, it would be a good practice to avoid constructing command strings directly from user input when possible.

To address this vulnerability, consider validating and sanitizing the host_name input before incorporating it into the ssh_cmd string or utilizing parameterized queries if applicable.
</analysis>

