1. Command Injection (CWE-78) - Medium Confidence:
The function executes an SSH command by using the `ssh_cmd` variable which is constructed from user input (cmd). Although it doesn't directly use this data in the SQL query, there is still a risk that an attacker could manipulate the cmd parameter to inject malicious commands during execution. To mitigate this vulnerability, validate and sanitize user input before using it to construct command strings.

