- `R`: Remote IP address
- `T`: Time (current time or time at which the request was accepted)
- `u`: Username (authenticated user)

Some tokens have additional options specified in braces, such as:

- `%{token:option}`: This is used to specify an option for the token. For example, `%T` on its own refers to the current time, but if you use it as `%{T:custom_format}`, it will use the specified custom format instead of the default one.
- `%%%c`: This is a placeholder for the actual character specified in the input string (useful when formatting complex strings with placeholders).

The function also supports nested braces, but this is not demonstrated in the provided code. The function returns 0 on success and -1 on failure or if there's an error in the access log format.

